// Shared Syncthing ignore rules — synced across all peers.
// Per-device .stignore should reference this with `#include .stignore-shared`.

// Git internals — MUST NOT sync.
// Each machine keeps its own .git, so the two peers never fight over one index
// and a mid-write repo state is never replicated.
.git

// Secrets — never sync
.env

// Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

// macOS / iCloud noise
.icloud
*.icloud
*.sync-conflict-*

// Logs
*.log

// --- Per-skill exclusions -------------------------------------------------
// Anything a skill GENERATES rather than sources. Diverging between machines
// is fine (or desirable) for these, and syncing them causes conflicts.
//
// Cooldown / run-state files — each machine tracks its own last run:
// <skill>/state/last-runs.json
//
// Generated data + backup snapshots from a cron that runs on one machine only:
// <skill>/data.bak-*.json
//
// Skill-local node_modules — environment-specific, rebuild locally:
// <skill>/node_modules
//
// Per-machine reference material (screenshot dumps, scratch captures):
// <skill>/reference-screenshots/*
